  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Leo has already won the Ballon d'Or 888 times, so he is really impressed with it (is he?).\n\nLeo has an array AAA containing NNN integers. Each element of this array is either 111 or 222.\n\nHe wants to figure out if the product of all the elements of the array can be written as an 888-th power of some integer, i.e, k8k^8k8 for some integer kkk.\n\nPrint `Yes` if it can and `No` if it can't.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN  — the number of integers in Leo's array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, denoting the elements of array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line `\"YES\"` if a valid kkk exists, and `\"No\"` otherwise (without quotes).\n\n\nEach letter of the output may be printed in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e, the strings `no`, `No`, `nO`, and `NO` will all be treated as equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤21 \\leq A_i \\leq 21≤Ai​≤2",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n1\n2\n9\n2 2 2 2 1 2 2 2 2",
        "output": "NO\nYES",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The product of the array is 222, which can't be written as k8k^8k8 for any integer kkk. So, the answer is No.\nTest case 222: The product of the array is 2×2×2×2×1×2×2×2×2=2562\\times 2\\times 2\\times 2\\times 1\\times 2\\times 2\\times 2\\times 2 = 2562×2×2×2×1×2×2×2×2=256, which equals 282^828. So, the answer is Yes."
      }
    ]
  },
